  "chapter_endings": [
    "Behind me, through the cold glass, the pond held the last grey light and gave none of it back.",
    "Then I went back to the lamplight and lay down in my coat, and listened to a house that, when I held still, didn't seem to be holding quite as still as I was.",
    "Pressed deep, the shape of someone, as if I had never sat at all.",
    "The count went on behind the wall while I wrote, and I didn't let myself hear which number it had reached.",
    "Then I logged it on the manifest in my own hand, the contents listed and the seal described, the way I described every chest in every house I had ever emptied, and I had no reason yet to know that the manifest was the one document in Coldmere I would come to trust the least.",
    "Then I went out and pulled the door to behind me, and waited in the cold of the passage with my pen in my hand and my lot list filled, and the one room in the house I couldn't rule a line under at my back."
